<title>USA: U.S. inspection destinations for wheat/corn/barley.</title>
<headline>U.S. inspection destinations for wheat/corn/barley.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-10-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>USDA said the 26.287 million bushels wheat, 29.854 million bushels of corn and 473,000 bushels of barley inspected in the week to Oct 3 included the following destinations (1,000 bu):</p>
<p>WHEAT: Lakes to Algeria 1,266; Belgium 92; Greece 497;</p>
<p>Italy 1,340; United Kingdom 604; Venezuela 637.</p>
<p>Gulf to Colombia 604; Costa Rica 523; Egypt 2,021; El</p>
<p>Salvador 165; Ethiopia 39; Guatemala 879; Kenya 658; Mexico</p>
<p>733; Peru 849; Senegal 81.</p>
<p>Pacific to Japan 2,649; South Korea 1,394; Pakistan</p>
<p>3,472; Philippines 1,350; Singapore 445; Yemen 1,062.</p>
<p>CORN: Gulf to Algeria 1,213; Angola 464; Taiwan 2,315;</p>
<p>Colombia 754; Costa Rica 276; El Salvador 63; Guatemala 98;</p>
<p>Israel 1,972; Japan 6,021; South Korea 2,063; Malaysia 2,009;</p>
<p>Mexico 5,253; Panama 334; Peru 1,012; Saudi Arabia 1,067;</p>
<p>Senegal 193; United Arab Emirates 1,006.</p>
<p>Pacific to Taiwan 2,068.</p>
<p>Interior to Mexico 596.</p>
<p>BARLEY: Pacific to Japan 473.</p>
</text>
